4. GENERAL INFORMATION ON THE 2024 CENSUS
Introduction
The Papua New Guinea (PNG) National Population Census is the most important national event in the
calendar of the country every ten years. In the month of June 2024, the 5th National Population Census was
held. The first full census for the country was in 1980, the second in 1990, followed by the third and fourth in
2000 and 2011 respectively.
The importance of the national census cannot be over emphasized. Without accurate population figures,
all planning and programs risk being ineffective or futile. The Government of PNG through the National
Executive Council (NEC) Decision No. 81/2019 endorsed the need for the conduct of a National Population
Census in the year 2020, however due to the global pandemic that affected the country in March 2020, the
NEC (Decision No.194/2020) approved to defer the conduct of the census to 2021. Subsequently, another
surge of the COVID 19 cases in April 2021 led to further deferment of the census to the most feasible and
earlier date being 2024 as endorsed in NEC Decision No. 174/2021.
The Government through the NEC instructed the National Statistical Office (NSO) to conduct the 5th National


