2024 National Population Census Final Figures
30
helps identify areas not covered. It is also useful for the dissemination of the final census results.
The census covered over 30,000 census units (including villages and communities in urban and rural areas),
spanning 22 provinces, 98 districts, 369 LLGs, and more than 6,400 wards.
Data Limitatiion
The report contains population figures based on where people were counted at census time (Sunday 16th
June 2024), which may not have been where they usually live. All provinces were visited and successfully
counted.
Comparison with other previous censuses should be made with caution because of the differences in the
operational strategies and coverage, and definition changes which have been progressively implemented at
censuses since 1966.

